{"t":21346,"op":"edit","agent":"A","path":"factory/questions.json","vstart":2,"vend":3,"lines":["  \"about\": \"The three Jev question sets the Flock puts to `POST /v1/systemone`: `flock_step`, read by factory/flock/step_reading.mjs once per green story step; `flock_resolve`, read by factory/flock/engine.mjs at a merge conflict an agent resolves; and `flock_release`, read by factory/flock/engine.mjs at a task given back. Each names its reader and its rollback (map #1131 rule 3). A question is literal: it names no policy word, and nothing here decides anything. Their modes live in factory/policy.json's `flock.jev_step`, `flock.jev_resolve` and `flock.jev_release`. A Jev `null` routes that reading to the set's stated rollback, never to a guess. A reworded question is a different question: its readings mean something else.\","]}
{"t":27744,"op":"edit","agent":"A","path":"factory/questions.json","vstart":32,"vend":32,"lines":["    },","    \"flock_resolve\": {","      \"when\": \"When an agent resolves a merge conflict in a file of its copy, once per resolve\",","      \"reader\": \"factory/flock/engine.mjs\",","      \"rollback\": \"factory/policy.json flock.jev_resolve.mode = off\",","      \"state\": [","        \"path\",","        \"annotated\",","        \"tasks\"","      ],","      \"provenance\": \"factory review reading 2026-09-29 (Jev candidate 1); operator pick 2026-09-29\",","      \"calibrated\": false,","      \"questions\": {","        \"already_joined\": {","          \"type\": \"choice\",","          \"instructions\": {","            \"question\": \"In `annotated`, do the left and right sides of each conflict already fit together as the merged text shows them, so the file needs no edit?\",","            \"context\": \"`annotated` is the merged file, with each conflict shown as a `<<<<<<<` / `=======` / `>>>>>>>` section holding its left and right sides. `path` is the file. `tasks` are the titles of the tasks that touch it.\"","          },","          \"criteria\": {","            \"no_edit_needed\": \"Both sides say things that stand together as merged\",","            \"needs_edit\": \"One side's meaning is lost, or the text does not read as one file, until someone edits it\",","            \"contradictory\": \"The two sides want opposite things, and one must be chosen\"","          }","        }","      }","    },","    \"flock_release\": {","      \"when\": \"When an agent gives its task back to the board, once per release\",","      \"reader\": \"factory/flock/engine.mjs\",","      \"rollback\": \"factory/policy.json flock.jev_release.mode = off\",","      \"state\": [","        \"task\",","        \"title\",","        \"files\",","        \"reason\",","        \"depends_on\"","      ],","      \"provenance\": \"factory review reading 2026-09-29 (Jev candidate 2); operator pick 2026-09-29\",","      \"calibrated\": false,","      \"questions\": {","        \"blocker\": {","          \"type\": \"choice\",","          \"instructions\": {","            \"question\": \"Given `reason`, what stands between this task and its facts passing?\",","            \"context\": \"`task` and `title` name the task. `files` are the files it may change. `reason` is what the agent said when it gave the task back. `depends_on` are the tasks it depends on.\"","          },","          \"criteria\": {","            \"fixable\": \"Another attempt at `files` could make them pass\",","            \"waiting_on_peer\": \"They need work another task in `depends_on` or elsewhere has not published yet\",","            \"plan_defect\": \"No change to `files` can make them pass as the plan states them\"","          }","        }","      }"]}
